{"lines":[{"h":0.01466497230396302,"t":"Test 1","w":0.050226287841796877,"c":1,"y":0.059527978938126114,"x":0.084748447691283382},{"x":0.384083045381576,"w":0.1193771616617838,"c":1,"y":0.10610465086935972,"t":"READING","h":0.01744186102384615},{"c":1,"x":0.084775086727269314,"w":0.25778546651204431,"y":0.17004898526789258,"h":0.016095171448565537,"t":"READING PASSAGE 1"},{"x":0.084775080427192881,"w":0.70588236490885425,"c":1,"t":"You should spend about 20 minutes on Questions 1-13, which are based on Reading","y":0.20783764874941624,"h":0.018906537263521983},{"h":0.017494751574527623,"c":1,"w":0.14532872517903647,"y":0.2267319801910983,"t":"Passage 1 below.","x":0.084775083671391749},{"c":1,"h":0.021802325612435891,"y":0.26162790695283844,"w":0.2768166097005208,"x":0.30795847705285384,"t":"The Davies Sisters"},{"h":0.017565951470814967,"w":0.68512110392252601,"y":0.3051084674107446,"c":1,"t":"Between 1908 and 1924, Gwendoline and Margaret Davies amassed one of","x":0.10553633375587718},{"t":"the largest collections of late-nineteenth and early-twentieth-century French","x":0.10380622423908667,"y":0.32400279917355879,"w":0.68339101155598958,"c":1,"h":0.017566968545453143},{"y":0.34149755084552491,"x":0.36332180155205968,"w":0.16608996073404941,"h":0.017514077327399957,"t":"paintings in Britain","c":1},{"w":0.70597422281901046,"x":0.084726747537032354,"h":0.019144342527930069,"y":0.37777634985441066,"t":"Gwendoline (1882-1951) and Margaret (1884-1963) Davies were the granddaughters","c":1},{"y":0.3947239258813775,"t":"of David Davies, a Welshman who amassed a fortune in the shipping and mining","w":0.65580266316731772,"h":0.021356415131277284,"c":1,"x":0.082997857506891343},{"h":0.018925863016394207,"c":1,"w":0.7231833902994792,"y":0.4142441860723034,"t":"industries. In 1907, when Gwendoline came into her inheritance (Margaret would follow","x":0.083044982882747906},{"c":1,"x":0.082997753848000858,"y":0.43134358711675691,"w":0.69905583699544271,"h":0.020888845765398734,"t":"in 1909), the sisters were said to be the wealthiest unmarried women in Britain. Their"},{"c":1,"x":0.083044990621988668,"w":0.70242212931315107,"y":0.45203488343936304,"h":0.017524248741155213,"t":"religious upbringing in rural Wales gave them a deep sense of social responsibility and"},{"y":0.46947674421260943,"c":1,"t":"they chose to use their inheritance for cultural and philanthropic* purposes.","h":0.018976719417798882,"w":0.62110727945963551,"x":0.083044976120311045},{"h":0.022854206360162221,"c":1,"t":"While there was no real family history of art collecting, the sisters' education was","y":0.50380043921215245,"x":0.08469917870571389,"w":0.65586975097656253},{"t":"rigorously geared toward such pursuits. Their London school focused on cultural rather","h":0.01744186102384615,"c":1,"w":0.71280278523763019,"y":0.5247093020438971,"x":0.083044974070244748},{"x":0.082976206204276939,"w":0.7008574930826823,"c":1,"h":0.022468900580436268,"t":"than academic study, and they travelled extensively with their governess, Jane Blaker,","y":0.54043350564205384},{"w":0.59169550577799468,"c":1,"t":"visiting art galleries and making extensive notes on the collections there.","x":0.08304498061703465,"y":0.56088173555185072,"h":0.019060124877118167},{"x":0.083044990017663453,"h":0.019008250733703158,"y":0.59727081899993562,"t":"The sisters began to make regular art purchases from 1908, which roughly coincided","c":1,"w":0.68685119628906255},{"h":0.022030784334645892,"w":0.67656224568684897,"t":"with the dates of their inheritance. They took advice from various people, including","x":0.08300397814933215,"c":1,"y":0.61462723509877382},{"w":0.68524983723958333,"h":0.020565778413296099,"c":1,"t":"the art dealer Hugh Blaker (the brother of Jane Blaker) and David Croal Thompson,","x":0.082986504445760265,"y":0.63218674613034131},{"t":"who was also an art dealer. While it was long assumed that these men were largely","x":0.08304498367933888,"h":0.017503905913644591,"c":1,"y":0.65255423389798517,"w":0.66955017089843749},{"h":0.021946301737225449,"x":0.082995026149691661,"c":1,"w":0.68868118286132807,"t":"responsible for the nature of the sisters' collection, it has recently been accepted that","y":0.66852842510652144},{"w":0.58491882324218747,"y":0.68877325712165804,"c":1,"x":0.084703860991825627,"t":"Gwendoline and Margaret retained a far more active role in the process.","h":0.020416350528191129},{"y":0.72529069770143872,"w":0.71799306233723958,"t":"The sisters' journals reveal their preference for Old Master** paintings. Yet they initially","h":0.018936034430149462,"x":0.083044991206775859,"c":1},{"w":0.67820068359374996,"h":0.018988925648202648,"x":0.083044990945339431,"c":1,"t":"made very few attempts to secure any such works. While the sisters were wealthy in","y":0.74273255793438353},{"w":0.67301035563151035,"h":0.017534420154910468,"c":1,"t":"relative terms, their income was nothing compared to the fortunes of American art","x":0.083044995102137115,"y":0.76308139506695893},{"x":0.083044981099364507,"t":"collectors of this period, such as J. Pierpont Morgan. Quite simply, high quality Old","y":0.78052325584192672,"w":0.67647059122721342,"h":0.018986890831554137,"c":1},{"x":0.08304498175219853,"t":"Master works were, if not beyond their means, then beyond what they were willing to","y":0.79941860432149647,"c":1,"w":0.69204152425130205,"h":0.020385454550249871},{"t":"pay for them. Instead, their early purchases were of the fashionable, safe variety, and","x":0.084720506396295622,"y":0.81619746469390875,"h":0.0211390714865618,"w":0.68696273803710939,"c":1},{"w":0.67128026326497403,"y":0.83575581397478893,"c":1,"h":0.019037747900330748,"x":0.083044989175132616,"t":"included, for example, paintings by the French artist Jean-Baptiste-Camille Corot."},{"t":"* philanthropic: seeking to promote the welfare of others, often by charitable funding","w":0.44982696533203126,"c":1,"x":0.084775098559611878,"h":0.011658421590496681,"y":0.92151162771842632},{"h":0.011651301400656511,"t":"** Old Master: a highly respected artist of great skill who worked in Europe before about 1800","y":0.93456962901360285,"w":0.49653981526692714,"x":0.084775074871537584,"c":1},{"y":0.95784883749852112,"h":0.014534882851794939,"c":1,"x":0.084775086796682456,"t":"16","w":0.020761245091756184}],"w":2400,"h":2857}